# Jupyter checkpoint/undo history. `.ipynb_checkpoints/<name>-checkpoint.ipynb` is a
# sibling copy of the notebook written on every autosave, and it captures the state
# of the last *executed* cell - so a key printed into a cell or a row pulled from a
# live table is preserved there even after being cleared from the notebook itself.
# The directory is rebuilt by Jupyter from the .ipynb on open, so nothing in it is
# ever the only copy of anything. (No .ipynb is tracked today.)
.ipynb_checkpoints/


