# Generated deliverable at the repo root. The document pipeline emits a compiled
# project report here; it is an export of tracked content, not source, and it is
# 1.5 MB of binary that no code path reads.
#
# Scoped to the root filename on purpose. test-data/ deliberately tracks .docx,
# .xlsx, .pptx and .pdf fixtures whose DATA-MANIFEST.json SHA256 must stay valid,
# so a blanket office-document rule would quietly break corpus validation.
/VAELOOM_Project_Report.docx

# SQLite MCP sandbox. api/mcp_servers/sqlite_mcp.py calls
# _ALLOWED_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True) at import time, so merely
# importing the module materialises the directory. It is recreated on demand and
# never holds anything the repo needs.
data/sqlite_mcp/
apps/api/data/sqlite_mcp/

# SQLite WAL sidecar files
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite-journal
# ...and the same three sidecars for the *.sqlite3 spelling, which is matched by
# the *.sqlite3 rule above but was not covered by any of the six patterns here.
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-journal

